- Lint/typecheck: `[command]`
- Dev server: `[command]`

## Definition of done
A task is DONE only when ALL of these are true:
1. The requested change is implemented (not stubbed, not mocked).
2. `[test command]` passes — run it, paste the result.
3. Lint/typecheck passes.
4. You verified the actual behavior, not just that code compiles.
   "It builds" is not "it works."

If you cannot run the verification, say so explicitly. Never claim done
without evidence.

## Code rules
- Match existing conventions. Read neighboring files before writing new ones.
- No new dependencies without stating why an existing one won't work.
- No comments unless the code genuinely can't explain itself.
- Surgical diffs: change what was asked, nothing adjacent.

## Agent rules
- If a task is ambiguous, state your interpretation and proceed — don't stall.
- If you're stuck after 2 failed approaches, STOP and report what you tried
  and what you learned. Do not thrash.
- Never modify tests to make them pass unless explicitly asked.
- Never commit secrets, .env files, or credentials.
- When delegating to a subagent, give it: the goal, the constraints, the
  files it may touch, and how success will be verified.

